# Owlry web app — environment.
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. With these UNSET, the app runs entirely
# local (IndexedDB) exactly as it does today; setting them lights up the
# Supabase backend (XP / ink / coins / calendar / radar served from the server).
#
# The anon key is a PUBLIC key — safe to ship to the browser; Row-Level
# Security is what actually protects the data.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-PUBLIC-KEY

# ── the live owl chat ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The owl's brain runs in the `owl-chat` Supabase edge function. The model
# key is a SERVER-SIDE Supabase secret — NEVER shipped to the browser.
#
# Pick the model vendor with OWL_PROVIDER (default: anthropic):
#   Claude:  supabase secrets set OWL_PROVIDER=anthropic ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#   Gemini:  supabase secrets set OWL_PROVIDER=gemini    GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...
# then deploy:
#   supabase functions deploy owl-chat
# Switching vendor is just changing OWL_PROVIDER (keep both keys to flip back).
# Models live in supabase/functions/owl-chat/owl-system.ts
# (OWL_MODEL = claude-sonnet-4-6, OWL_GEMINI_MODEL = gemini-2.5-flash).
#
# With a backend configured, the live owl answers by default. To force
# the offline mockup brain everywhere (e.g. for demos), set:
# VITE_OWL_LIVE=off
#
# (Users can also flip live ⇄ classic any time in Settings → THE OWL.)
